Builds the rust codec for Android with the NDK the rest of Skia uses (r27).

Skia's Bazel Android toolchain downloads NDK r21e. Skia 157's core, which
//rust/png:ffi_rs pulls in through //rust/common:ffi_utils, now uses C++20
library features that r21e's libc++ (LLVM 9) lacks: 36 files of src/core
fail with "no template named 'to_array' in namespace 'std'". The GN build of
the same sources uses NDK r27d and is fine.

This points the Bazel toolchain at that same NDK instead of downloading one.
scripts/build_skia.ps1 sets SKIA_PREP_ANDROID_NDK to the NDK root it passes to
GN as `ndk`; a local repository rule symlinks it as @ndk_linux_amd64. The
module extension is reproducible, so MODULE.bazel.lock records neither it nor
the path. The toolchain files move to the r27 layout: sysroot and libc++ under
toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64/sysroot, no GCC toolchain (clang
--target=<triple><api>), binutils trampolines replaced by llvm-ar, ld.lld and
friends, clang 18's resource directory. The API level is 26, the package's
ndk_api (minSdk), instead of 29.

One NDK per package also means one libc++: with r21e, the rust archive carried
r21e's libc++ objects next to the consumer's r27d libc++.

Checked on Skia 157 (b94213a11b, chrome/m157) under WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04, NDK r27d.

